- net
- pass

' A world's door. A session is a secret that whoever is at the door keeps
' and shows; the world keeps only its hash. A session opens the door when
' the world keeps a grant for it: the hash and when it ends, signed by the
' custody the world's own card states. So the key that merely runs a world
' opens nothing, and a grant made before custody moved opens nothing after.
' These are the rules, pure. The grant is signed at the foot's desk
' (desk.foil); the secret is hashed where a request is parsed and goes no
' further (http_foot/session).
+ door
  + named
    ' The name a session goes by: the hash of its secret.
    \ secret=str
    ^ nat
    = bytes (str/to_atom secret)
    | Sha256 (add bytes (bex (mul 8 secret.len)))
  + at
    ' Where a session's grant is kept.
    \ self=iota session=nat
    ^ path
    [self 'io 'door ($x session)]
  + grant
    ' A grant as the record that keeps it.
    \ g=pass/grant
    ^ myth
    | (myth/sing ['until] (pails/n g.until)).put(['sig] (pails/n g.sig))
  + open
    ' Whether a session opens this world's door now.
    \ session=nat now=nat state=namespace
    ^ bool
    = self state.self
      me (quip_val self)
      home=path [self 'io 'mesa]
      custody (net/held ['custody] home state)
    ? (eq 0 session) .false
    ? (eq 0 custody) .false
    ?> (./some record) (sovereign_care .x (door/at self session) state).fil .false
    = g (pass/grant me session record.nat_at(['until] 0) record.nat_at(['sig] 0))
      stands (pass/standing 0 0 0 0 0 custody)
    | either/is_ok (pass/allowed me stands now g)
